<title>BELGIUM: Belgian state railways 1996 profit surges.</title>
<headline>Belgian state railways 1996 profit surges.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(In billion of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				 2.182 vs	  0.506</p>
<p>    Current profit			   1.203 vs   loss 5.123</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total		  330, up 8.1 percent</p>
<p>    Total debt			     131     vs	119</p>
<p>    Exceptional gains			0.979 vs	n/a</p>
<p>    Investments			     49.305 vs	 38.147</p>
<p>NOTE - Belgian NMBS/SNCB state railways said in a statement that 20.53 billion of the investments were aimed for the HST fast-train network and 28.78 billion for the domestic network.</p>
<p>It said the improvement of the current result was due to the execution of measures of the &quot;Target 2005&quot; restructuring and investment plan, which is aimed at making the company profitable by the year 2005.</p>
<p>It added its financial result had improved by 1.15 billion francs following a better forex coverage and further slide in interest rates.</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815</p>
</text>
